> . We considered three different approaches in total for how to build the RegexCaseEquivalence table:

I guess case folding would be a 4th possible approach - which could be considered in future - unless that's the same thing as "linguistic comparison".

@mkArtakMSFT when preparing a response to a web request, does the server generally set CurrentCulture to the culture of the client? We are preparing a change that could potentially modify the behavior of regex objects when they are constructed with CurrentCulture X and consumed in CurrentCulture Y. The current behavior is stable but quite incoherent (it depends on things like the exact pattern, see #36147), and this would make it much more coherent (as well as faster). I think we have to make this change but I'm curious how common it is to create and use regexes in this way.

